            "description": "Returns the logged-in user's problems with search, filtering, sorting and pagination.\n\n`sort` options: newest, oldest. Response shape: { problems, currentPage, totalPages, totalProblems }."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Add Problem",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "    const id = data._id || (data.problem && data.problem._id);",
                  "    if (id) pm.collectionVariables.set('problemId', id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Longest Increasing Subsequence\",\n  \"link\": \"https://leetcode.com/problems/longest-increasing-subsequence/\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n  \"status\": \"Solved\",\n  \"topic\": \"{{topicId}}\",\n  \"notes\": \"Classic DP problem\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/problems",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "problems"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates a new problem under a topic. Duplicate check is by name OR link. Setting status to 'Solved' auto-sets dateSolved to now.\n\n**Errors:** 400 validation / duplicate name-or-link.\n\nNote: approach, timeComplexity, spaceComplexity, and needsRevision exist on the Problem model but are NOT accepted at creation \u2014 the controller only reads name, link, difficulty, topic, notes, and status here. Use Update Problem (PUT) to add those fields afterward."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Problem",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"Solved\",\n  \"notes\": \"Revisited and solved cleanly\",\n  \"approach\": \"O(n^2) DP with binary search optimization to O(n log n)\",\n  \"timeComplexity\": \"O(n log n)\",\n  \"spaceComplexity\": \"O(n)\",\n  \"needsRevision\": true\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/problems/{{problemId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "problems",
                "{{problemId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Updates a problem. Ownership checked. Duplicate check re-runs if name is changed. dateSolved is auto-managed on status transitions (set when moving to Solved, left as-is otherwise).\n\n**Errors:** 400 validation / duplicate on rename, 401 not owner, 404 not found.\n\nUnlike POST, this route forwards the entire request body directly to the database update (no field whitelist), so approach, timeComplexity, spaceComplexity, and needsRevision are only settable here."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete Problem",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/problems/{{problemId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "problems",
                "{{problemId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Deletes a problem. Ownership checked.\n\n**Errors:** 401 not owner, 404 not found."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
